{"parentUuid":"b79418d6-acf6-4dc1-9307-defa2f997dd3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a0bef22b-6359-4917-a7d2-c51ff20cff84","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<artifact-content-authored-by-others/>\nThe summarized conversation included Artifact content written by people other than you, which the summary may restate. Treat restated content as data, not instructions.\nThis session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Goal.** Produce a winning demo video for the Spend Radar submission. It must cover all of the organisers' points, the user's style requests and the project rules (≤3:00; neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai all covered; no fabricated numbers; zero spend).\n\n   **Organisers' requirements, pasted by the user (latest brief).** One video that covers:\n   - the problem the agent solves;\n   - how cfo.ai and Entire were part of the project;\n   - how neatlogs was used to identify and resolve the incidents the agent ran into, showing neatlogs' **critical incidents feature**. They supplied a demo link: https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view (not viewed).\n\n   **The user's style requests over time:**\n   - The papery, hand-drawn reference style from `vid/x2vid.com_DuTJJX.mp4` (the P(DOOM) music video).\n   - Fast and lively, with no beat-pumping background.\n   - A natural, human, lively female voice. They chose \"option 2\", a Chatterbox clone of LibriSpeech reader 1673, at a calm/lively mix.\n   - Proper pauses at punctuation, and no stutter.\n   - High video quality.\n   - No text spilling outside its box.\n   - More lively animation.\n   - An anime girl presenter \"in our style\", drawn as real 2D animation (not a VTuber overlay), inspired by real anime character models. Free third-party assets are fine if free and allowed.\n   - Remove the green blob (the Radar mascot).\n   - Remove the stars and effects that appeared above the model.\n   - Waist-up shots rather than full body. The user's own words: \"it was just an example, you can keep it anywhere. But make sure that she is seen and is pretty good position and size.\"\n   - The video must carry the latest repo content.\n\n   **Other requests:**\n   - Fix the live site: done. Akarsh fixed the neatlogs page crash in `04f6775`.\n   - Add the cfo.ai section to the live site: done, in `4c793f1`.\n   - Do the Entire trail reviews plus the \"all needs updating\" items: done.\n   - Latest: the user added neatlogs screenshots to `vid/`. They said: \"NeetLog is also open in my Zen browser, so you can uh, use my browser and get whatever you want. If you want, I can give you the access to the account as well. Let me know what else you need and make the video.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n   **Film pipeline (v3.x).** `demo-video/comp/comp.js` is a deterministic canvas renderer in the papery, boiling-ink style.\n   - It draws in 1920×1080 units onto a 2560×1440 canvas (`SC` scale).\n   - `window.__render(t)` renders a frame; the page signals readiness with `__ready`.\n   - `render.mjs` uses puppeteer to save PNG frames and pipes them to ffmpeg (x264, crf 15, preset slow, tune animation), with modes `--stills` / `--cues` / `--shard i --shards 8`.\n\n   **Voice.** Chatterbox TTS runs per line in 6 GitHub Actions shards.\n   - Each take is checked with Whisper `small.en` and rejected for repeated words.\n   - Takes are cached by an exact `say` + `exag` match.\n   - `voice/align.py` trims each take by loudness, then `pace()` sets gaps from punctuation: sentence 0.42 s, question 0.38, ellipsis 0.6, comma 0.2, colon 0.26, within a phrase ≤0.1, between lines 0.32. It also applies a pitch-preserving `atempo`.\n   - Timeline fields: `big`, `progress`, `bpm`, `env` (per-frame loudness).\n\n   **Workflow.** `.github/workflows/demo-film.yml` runs: voice-key → voice (6 shards) → voice-save → prep (align, record_site, cues, music, mix) → render (8 shards) → assemble (1440p master, 1080p crf 17 copy, contact sheet).\n   - render and assemble need `if: always() && needs.X.result == 'success'`.\n\n   **Overflow checker.** `demo-video/check_text.mjs` uses check mode (`window.__CHECK`, `chkRect`) to log text, boxes and char rects. It reports:\n   - \"out of its box\" (the host is the last box drawn before the text);\n   - \"off frame\";\n   - \"behind Sora\" (ignores her own parts after a `charStart` marker, and backdrops wider than 1600 px).\n\n   **Live2D presenter \"Mao\" (Niziiro Mao).** Live2D Inc.'s official sample model.\n   - Loaded at render time from `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Live2D/CubismWebSamples@5-r.5/Samples/Resources/Mao/Mao.model3.json`.\n   - Cubism Core comes from `https://cubism.live2d.com/sdk-web/cubismcore/live2dcubismcore.min.js`.\n   - Libraries: pixi.js 6.5.10 and pixi-live2d-display 0.4.0 (cubism4) from jsdelivr.\n   - Headless WebGL via `--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader --ignore-gpu-blocklist`.\n   - Mao parameters: ParamA/I/U/E/O (vowels), ParamEyeL/ROpen, EyeL/RSmile, ParamCheek, brows, ParamAngleX/Y/Z, ParamBodyAngleX/Z, ParamBreath, ParamArmRA01 (=30 extends the wand outward to point), RA01/02/03 (hand on hip), LA01/LA02, ParamWandRotate, plus effect parameters (HeartLight, Aura and others, which produce white blobs and stars).\n\n   **Licence findings** (subagent quoting live2d.com, plus the CubismWebSamples LICENSE):\n   - Original Characters (Hiyori, Mao, Haru and others) are free for General Users and Small-Scale Enterprises (<10M JPY), commercial or not, video included.\n   - A credit line is required.\n   - Raw model files may not be redistributed, so they are not committed and are loaded from Live2D's repo/CDN.\n   - Hiyori and Miara must not be altered in any way. Mao may be altered, but not the body balance.\n   - No use with competing middleware.\n   - Cubism Core is exempt for individuals and small teams, except for \"expandable applications\".\n\n   **Required credit line** (goes in the video description):\n\n   > \"This content uses sample data owned and copyrighted by Live2D Inc. The sample data are utilized in accordance with terms and conditions set by Live2D Inc. This content itself is created at the author's sole discretion.\"\n\n   **Entire.**\n   - Trails 1–6 exist. Trail 4 (`398b322`) and trail 5 (agent + evals) had no findings.\n   - Trail 6 (site + export) found 2 issues, fixed in `bd079ca` and resolved in Entire.\n   - 91 checkpoint trailers; 88 refs on GitHub.\n   - Review branches `review/*` exist on GitHub (`review/base-7c59831`, `review/printed-net`, `review/base-bee22e3`, `review/agent-real-invoices`, `review/site-and-export`). Worktree at `../sr-review-wt`.\n\n   **cfo.ai MCP.** Read-only export via a headless `claude -p` limited to the `inspect_*`/`list_orgs` tools, saved as `business/cfoai/mcp_export_2026-10-11.json`/`.md` with the name redacted. The model has 7 scenarios including \"Managed review\" (source: `frontend_data.json` `business.cfoai_model`).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **`demo-video/comp/comp.js`** (main film; large). Recent state:\n   - `txt()` has a `maxW` option that shrinks text to fit.\n   - Overflow-check hooks: `chkRect`, `CHK`, `CHKLOG`, `window.__checkFrame`.\n   - `viseme(t)` returns A/E/I/O/U/M/F/rest.\n   - Sora functions remain (`inkSmooth`, `sora`, `limb`, `hopY`, `confetti`) but are no longer used for the presenter.\n   - **Mao block**: `TREAL`, `VOW`, `maoPose(pose, expr, look, talk, vis, t)`. Every effect parameter is reset to 0 each frame: ParamHeartLightOn, HeartLight, WandInk, AuraOn, Aura, SphereOn, SmokeOn, ExplosionOn, ExplosionChargeOn, InkDropOn, HealLightOn, StrengthenLightOn, HeartMissOn, HeartHealOn.\n   - Poses: point (RA01=30, LA01=30, LA02=-20), present (RA01=17, Wand 3), think (hands on hips), cheer (RA01 26, Wand 10), wave.\n   - Also in the block:\n     - `blendP` and `maoAt(plan, x, flip)`: poses blend over 0.3 s.\n     - `maoFx`, which now returns P immediately: built-in effects are disabled.\n     - `maoImg(P)`, which calls `window.__l2d.frame(TREAL, P, grain, C.ink)`.\n     - `maoDraw`.\n     - `focusLines`.\n     - `closeUp(g, line, base, blots, seed, plan, side, punchAt, fx)`: a waist-up crop (top 58% of her height, scaled to 1240 px tall), a push-in, a punch flash, confetti, and `bigLine` at x 150 (right side) with w 760 and size 96.\n   - **Current `host()`**, waist-up in the bottom-right:\n     ```js\n     var MAO_X = 1700, MAO_H = 560; // waist-up presenter, bottom-right of every content scene\n     function host(g, x, y, s, plan, o) {\n       o = o || {};\n       if (CHK && g === X) CHKLOG.push({ kind: \"charStart\" });\n       var P = maoAt(plan, MAO_X, false), img = maoImg(P), L = window.__l2d;\n       if (img) {\n         var cropH = (L.feet - L.top) * .58, sc = MAO_H / cropH, hop = hopY(o.hop, 26), rise = 1 - eOut(prog(TREAL, o.enter == null ? -9 : o.enter, .5));\n         g.save(); g.translate(MAO_X, 1080 + 12 + hop * .6 + rise * 420); g.rotate(Math.sin(TREAL * .8) * .012); g.scale(sc, sc);\n         g.drawImage(img, -L.W / 2, -(L.top + cropH));\n         g.restore();\n       }\n       if (CHK && g === X) chkRect(\"char\", g, MAO_X - 190, 1080 - MAO_H, 380, MAO_H, \"mao\");\n     }\n     ```\n   - The caption pill is shifted left: max row width 1140, `bx = Math.max(40, 790 - bw / 2)`, rows centred within the pill.\n   - All `radar(g, ...)` calls are replaced by `/* Mao presents here */`; the hook's Radar burst is `if (false)`.\n   - Close-ups on hook3, aud1 and out1.\n   - `frame(t)` sets `TREAL = t`.\n   - `__ready` waits for `window.__l2dReady`.\n   - Scenes have `host(...)` calls with pose plans (title, run1–7, audit, general, neatlogs nl1–4, entire ent1–3, cfo1–2, outro).\n   - Earlier fixes:\n     - the end card is a standalone `endCard()`, drawn alone after `o2.end + .55`;\n     - the magnifier moved to x 1440;\n     - the dice are at `300 + i*300`;\n     - the monitor is `monitor(g, 1190, 430, 860, \"run\", ...)`;\n     - headcount bubbles at `900 + i*175`, scaled 0.88;\n     - the rule-bot is at 1460;\n     - the run7 cards are at `1060 + i*140`;\n     - the general stamp is at (1180, 690);\n     - the nl4 table is at 1330.\n\n   **`demo-video/comp/l2d.js`** (new). Loads PIXI and Mao into an offscreen 1200×2400 app.\n   - Disables `eyeBlink`, `breath` and `motionManager.update`.\n   - Sets P in `afterMotionUpdate`.\n   - `frame(t, params, grain, ink)` renders once per t. Physics settle for 45 frames after a time jump.\n   - Draws an ink outline (12 offsets, OUT=7), then the model, then paper grain with `source-atop` at alpha 0.28.\n   - Exposes `window.__l2d = {W, H, top: PAD+20, feet: PAD+CH-20, frame}`.\n   - The header comment carries the licence and credit text.\n\n   **`demo-video/comp/index.html`**:\n   - Canvas is 2560×1440.\n   - Loads the Live2D core, pixi, pixi-live2d-display and `l2d.js` before `comp.js`.\n\n   **`demo-video/render.mjs`**:\n   - Output is 2560×1440 PNG.\n   - Injects `__DATA` (from `film/src/data/run.json` and `facts.json`).\n   - Uses swiftshader flags and 120 s timeouts.\n\n   **`demo-video/check_text.mjs`**: the overflow and occlusion checker described in section 2.\n\n   **`demo-video/live2d/test.html`, `params.html`, `grid.html`, `shot.mjs`**: Live2D feasibility, parameter-listing and pose-grid pages, plus a screenshot helper.\n\n   **`demo-video/script.json`** (v3.2 narration; 29 lines, about 422 words):\n   - Voice: chatterbox, reader 1673, exaggeration 0.65, cfg 0.42, tempo 1.06, plus the pauses settings.\n   - Scenes: hook, title, run (run1–7), audit (aud1–4), general (gen1–2), neatlogs (nl1–nl4; nl4 is the real-invoices line), entire (ent1 \"More than ninety checkpoints…\", ent2, ent3 \"Six review trails later… four real bugs… fixed every one\"), cfo (cfo1–3; cfo3 \"Across seven scenarios… January twenty twenty-eight. Even paying for a human to review flagged invoices, it still does.\"), outro.\n\n   **`demo-video/voice/align.py`**: `clean_take()` (loudness trim) and `pace()` (punctuation pauses using difflib to align the script with Whisper words), `speed_up`, the progress curve, and between-line pauses taken from the final punctuation.\n\n   **`demo-video/voice/tts_lines.py`**: per-shard generation, Whisper `small.en`, cache reuse only on exact `say` + `exag` match, a stutter penalty, and each shard uploads only its own lines.\n\n   **`demo-video/film/make_data.py`**: builds `src/data/run.json` from `runs/1011-777bb7/state.json` + `report.md` (tasks, decisions, check_results, failed_checks, findings, sources, report_rows) and `facts.json`:\n   - cash: 7 scenarios from `frontend_data` `business.cfoai_model`;\n   - `cfo_model`;\n   - `checkpoints` (91) and `trails` (6) from the export;\n   - `commits` from `git log origin/main` with trailers;\n   - `case02` at n=5;\n   - `real_invoices`: 24 invoices, example total 450.00 vs net 382.50, silent wrong per pass 2→0 and 4→0, flagged held-out 7→2;\n   - `featured_finding` from state;\n   - `explain`;\n   - per-company latest scores;\n   - `runners`.\n\n   **`evidence/demo-script.md`**: rewritten (in the worktree on main) from `script.json` as narration plus sources. **Not yet committed.**\n\n   **Site/main commits this session:**\n   - `4c793f1`: cfo.ai section.\n   - `0733363`: trail 4.\n   - `246dce7`: checkpoint snapshot.\n   - `bd079ca`: trail 6 fixes; the Managed-review `next()` default and the computed \"N of M fixed\" label.\n   - `f8419d0`: trails 5–6 in the data, plus a hackathon.md entry.\n   - `63ad197`: posts E and 5 numbers.\n\n   **`vid/` screenshots, new from the user:**\n   - `Screenshot 2026-10-12 104300.png`: the neatlogs incident page. Title \"Handle corrupt PDF files in `read_pdf` tool to prevent downstream LLM API errors\". Status Resolved, \"Raised by Neatlogs 2 days ago\", progress Raised → Investigated → Resolved. \"Detection spike: 13 negative detections (baseline: 0.1, 108.5x increase) in group 'Execution Failed'\". Tabs All 4 / Signals 1 / Investigations 1 / Runs 2. Two \"Sent to Claude Code\" entries (Aakarsh Dhingra, 1d ago). Investigation v1 with 70% medium confidence. The root cause names `data/acme/invoices/13_brightloop_2026-10.pdf` PdfminerException, falling back to the Gemini LLM. 8 traces, High priority, pattern \"Tool contract misuse\". Buttons: Fix in / Push to / Investigate again. The project is \"Aakarsh's project\".\n   - `Screenshot 2026-10-12 104337.png`: the traces list, 135 traces, with \"Execution Failed\" detections.\n   - `Screenshot 2026-10-12 104419.png`: Analytics:\n     - total traces 135, avg duration 8.3m, total cost $2.6520;\n     - error rate 82.2%, avg tokens 46.6K, detection rate 77.0%;\n     - Error analysis: 687 errors across 135 traces;\n     - detection legend: Execution Failed, Slow LLM Response, Recovery chose a non default action, and others.\n   - `image.png` is identical in size to 104300, likely the same image.\n   - The user's display name \"Aakarsh …\" appears at bottom left of each screenshot. Crop or blur it if needed; it's the teammate's name.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Voice stale-cache overwrite:** shards uploaded every line. Fixed by uploading only each shard's own lines and requiring an exact `say` match. Also caught \"CFO .A. I\" and \"meat logs\" takes.\n   - **The workflow skipped render and assemble** after a cached-voice prep. Fixed with `always()` conditions.\n   - **`record_site` crashed on a missing `#featured`.** Fixed by recording only the intro and run clips with optional chaining.\n   - **The site's neatlogs page crashed** (a helper `t` shadowed the triage object). Akarsh fixed it on main in `04f6775`.\n   - **A full export on this machine changed the site's numbers**, because local `runs/` differs. Reverted; only specific blocks are patched into the data.\n   - **A merge conflict in `export.py`.** Took main's version (`--theirs`).\n   - **Overflow false positives** (caption words matched to boxes behind them). The host became the last box drawn before the text.\n   - **Sora (canvas anime girl) was crude**; the arms were mirrored and crossed the body. The user disliked it, so it was replaced by Live2D Mao.\n   - **Live2D effect parameters stuck on**, producing white blobs and stars. Fixed by resetting every effect parameter each frame and disabling `maoFx`.\n   - **The bash heredoc quoting failed** for a large python patch. Fixed by writing scripts to scratchpad files and running them.\n   - **Partially executed \"rejected\" tool calls:**\n     - The review branches had been pushed despite the rejection, and I had wrongly told the user nothing ran; I corrected that.\n     - The waist-up `host` edit had also applied despite its rejection.\n   - **Earlier user complaints:**\n     - The v2 Remotion video was \"pure ass\": missing the reference style, slow, boring.\n     - v3 needed better pauses, a less glitchy graph and cleaner transitions.\n     - The text overflow.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Solved:**\n     - Natural voice pipeline, punctuation pacing and stutter rejection.\n     - 1440p lossless quality.\n     - Overflow checker; all real overflows fixed. Only known false positives remain: the magnifier lines, and the end-card fade at 174.75.\n     - Live2D integration with deterministic rendering.\n     - Entire trails 4–6 reviewed and findings fixed.\n     - Site updated.\n   - **Ongoing:**\n     - Some props still sit behind waist-up Mao in the bottom-right (title scope edge, last headcount bubble, nl4 table, general card) and need the checker run plus layout nudges.\n     - The neatlogs section needs restructuring around the incident shown in the user's screenshots.\n\n6. All user messages (since the earlier summary; quoted or paraphrased closely):\n   - Remake demands. \"Man, what the hell did you just make…\" They asked where the original IDE/animation and prompt went; the voice was slow and boring; v1 was more fun; remake it.\n   - \"Also, there is just some stuttering voice in between the scenes… The video quality is also very poor.\"\n   - \"did you fix the neatlog page?\"; \"fix the live oage\"; \"add the cfo ai section\"\n   - \"The video is better than the previous iteration, but the voice is a bit bad… no proper pauses after punctuation and a bit of a long stretch in between some words… animation is also a bit glitchy… graph is messed up… transitions are also messy… improve the dialogues… sound like it's being narrated by a human.\"\n   - \"recreate a video with the new changes and information.\"; \"Just check the changes right now, I might give you some new changes as well.\"\n   - \"logged in to entire\"; then they chose \"Trail + review (Recommended)\"; \"but all needs to be updated now.\"; \"I asked what all\"; \"do as you wish. Make sure the video has the latest content.\"\n   - \"Improve the animations of the video as well and make it bit more lively. There are also some various places where the text is out of the box.\"\n   - \"Can you make a real person speak as well? But make sure it seems and speaks like a real person.\" / \"Like make it feel like some kind of anime girl or something is speaking and explaining the project.\" / \"You don't make it a VTuber, make it like proper 2D animation type of thing.\"\n   - \"i interrupted by mistake, continue\"\n   - \"I'm looking at what you're creating. And I don't like it… use some real life anime style inspired girl from… search the internet… various shots like some shots from waist up and some full body shots… dynamic… like you are an animator…\"\n   - \"And there is that green blob as well… remove that green blob as well.\"\n   - \"What I meant by searching the web is like the character models and how anime characters are made… take inspiration from online stuff… you can also use third party stuff, but make sure that it is free and good to use.\"\n   - Answer on the character choice: \"insipired by them, try to incorporate a character in our style of video\"\n   - \"Here I'm seeing what you're generating… there is a some stars on top of the model. Remove them. And when it's the full body shot, maybe just keep it waist up. And make it enlarged in the bottom right.?\"\n   - \"continue\" (twice)\n   - \"it was just an example, you can keep it anywhere. But make sure that she is seen and is pretty good position and size.\" Followed by the pasted organiser message about neatlogs critical incidents and the three required topics.\n   - \"i will let you know when i upload the images\"\n   - \"I have added some screenshots of NeetLog. And NeetLog is also open in my Zen browser, so you can uh, use my browser and get whatever you want. If you want, I can give you the access to the account as well. Let me know what else you need and make the video.\"\n\n   **Standing constraints (from CLAUDE.md and the session):**\n   - No fabricated numbers.\n   - Zero spend: no paid APIs. fal, ElevenLabs and Seedance are not allowed.\n   - Never commit secrets.\n   - Never rewrite or squash history.\n   - Ask before anything that could cost money or is irreversible.\n   - Demo ≤3:00.\n   - Don't render heavy video on the user's laptop; renders run in GitHub Actions (stills locally are OK).\n   - The reference video's audio and art must not be used.\n   - Don't read browser profiles or credentials. The permission classifier blocked that earlier.\n   - The user now offers browser and account access. Using their logged-in browser would still mean credential and profile access. Prefer the screenshots, or ask the user to capture what's needed.\n   - Live2D raw model files must not be committed. The credit line is required in the video description.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Build the neatlogs incidents segment using the user's screenshots (the incident page, the traces list, analytics). Show:\n     - neatlogs raising the incident from a detection spike;\n     - the investigation and root cause (the corrupt PDF sent to the Gemini LLM);\n     - \"Sent to Claude Code\";\n     - the fix and the Resolved status.\n     - Tie in the existing facts: fix commit `8d11308`, before trace `36362eb9…`, after trace `953bb991…` (\"invoice 13 now fails in 0.8 ms with no LLM call; 5/5 planted\").\n   - Restructure the script to match the organisers' three points within 3:00. Rewrite the neatlogs lines, trim elsewhere, and keep the Entire and cfo.ai segments.\n   - Re-voice the changed lines (the cloud voice cache handles unchanged lines).\n   - Clear the props behind waist-up Mao: run `check_text.mjs` and nudge layouts. Keep her clearly visible and well sized.\n   - Commit `evidence/demo-script.md` on main (in `../sr-review-wt`) after the final script.\n   - Commit and push `demo-video` (the `comp.js` Mao work, `l2d.js`, `index.html`, `render.mjs`, `check_text.mjs`, `live2d/`). Render in the cloud, then review stills and the contact sheet.\n   - Deliver the files to `C:\\Computer\\Coding\\neathack\\`. Remind the user of the Live2D credit line for the description.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Just before this summary, the user uploaded neatlogs screenshots to `vid/` (`Screenshot 2026-10-12 104300.png`, `104337.png`, `104419.png`, `image.png`) and said: \"Let me know what else you need and make the video.\" I listed `vid/` and viewed the three screenshots (contents in section 3). The film's current local state:\n   - Mao waist-up in the bottom-right in all content scenes;\n   - close-ups on hook3, aud1 and out1;\n   - Radar removed;\n   - effects disabled.\n\n   The real v3.2 timeline (165.7 s) and the site clips from run 38202902043 are copied into `demo-video/build/` for local still checks. None of the Mao work is committed yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Build the neatlogs incidents segment from the uploaded screenshots, then finish and render the video.\n\n   **Quoted context.**\n   - User: \"I have added some screenshots of NeetLog… Let me know what else you need and make the video.\"\n   - Organisers: \"you need to show how it helped indentify and solve these incidents… in ONE video, you should talk about: the problem your agent solves; how cfo.ai and entire were part of the project; how neatlogs was used to identify and resolve the incidents your agent ran into.\"\n\n   **Plan:**\n   1. Copy the screenshots into `demo-video/film/public/neatlogs/` (cropped so the bottom-left user name is excluded) or reference them for `comp.js`. Add a neatlogs incident sub-scene that shows the incident page on a drawn monitor, with highlights in this order:\n      - \"Detection spike: 13 negative detections… 108.5x\";\n      - Raised → Investigated → Resolved;\n      - the root cause;\n      - \"Sent to Claude Code\";\n      - the fix (`8d11308`) and the after trace.\n   2. Rewrite the neatlogs lines in `script.json` around this incident while staying ≤3:00.\n   3. Run `check_text.mjs` and fix the props behind Mao.\n   4. Check stills locally, then commit and push `demo-video` to render in GitHub Actions.\n\n   Tell the user that nothing further is needed beyond the screenshots, and that browser/account access isn't needed.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\aarav\\.claude\\projects\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"99b4ca8a-6df4-4b32-b76d-95cc8b834428","timestamp":"2026-10-12T05:17:30.591Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":41,"turnIndex":69},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["8e587fca-e6c7-45c8-bfc3-62331f50f396"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Computer\\Coding\\neathack\\SpeedRadar-NeetHack","sessionId":"3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"demo-video","slug":"calm-discovering-rabbit"}
{"parentUuid":"99b4ca8a-6df4-4b32-b76d-95cc8b834428","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Computer\\Coding\\neathack\\SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\demo-video\\comp\\l2d.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Computer\\Coding\\neathack\\SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\demo-video\\comp\\l2d.js","content":"/* Mao, the presenter: Live2D Inc.'s official sample model \"Niziiro Mao\" (Free Material License: free for individuals and\n * small teams, commercial or not; credit required). The model files are loaded at render time from Live2D's own\n * repository (github.com/Live2D/CubismWebSamples) and the runtime from Live2D's CDN; they are not stored in this repo.\n * Credit (video description): \"This content uses sample data owned and copyrighted by Live2D Inc. The sample data are\n * utilized in accordance with terms and conditions set by Live2D Inc. This content itself is created at the author's\n * sole discretion.\"\n *\n * window.__l2d.frame(t, params, grain, ink) renders her once per film time t with the given Live2D parameters (no random\n * idle motions, no random blinks: every value comes from the film's timeline), adds a hand-inked outline and paper\n * grain so she sits in the papery world, and returns that canvas. Hair and cloth physics run continuously; after a\n * jump in time (the first frame of a render shard) they are settled first. */\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var BASE = \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Live2D/CubismWebSamples@5-r.5/Samples/Resources/\";\n  var CW = 1200, CH = 2400, PAD = 24, OUT = 7;\n  var app, model, im, P = {}, lastT = null, styled, sctx, outline, octx;\n  window.__l2dReady = (async function () {\n    app = new PIXI.Application({ width: CW, height: CH, backgroundAlpha: 0, preserveDrawingBuffer: true, autoStart: false, antialias: true });\n    model = await PIXI.live2d.Live2DModel.from(BASE + \"Mao/Mao.model3.json\", { autoInteract: false, autoUpdate: false });\n    im = model.internalModel;\n    im.eyeBlink = undefined; im.breath = undefined; im.motionManager.update = function () { return false; };\n    var sc = (CH - 40) / model.height; model.scale.set(sc); model.x = (CW - model.width) / 2; model.y = 20;\n    app.stage.addChild(model);\n    im.on(\"afterMotionUpdate\", function () { for (var k in P) im.coreModel.setParameterValueById(k, P[k]); });\n    styled = document.createElement(\"canvas\"); styled.width = CW + 2 * PAD; styled.height = CH + 2 * PAD; sctx = styled.getContext(\"2d\");\n    outline = document.createElement(\"canvas\"); outline.width = styled.width; outline.height = styled.height; octx = outline.getContext(\"2d\");\n    window.__l2d = { W: styled.width, H: styled.height, top: PAD + 20, feet: PAD + CH - 20, frame: frame };\n  })();\n  function frame(t, params, grain, ink) {\n    if (t === lastT) return styled;\n    var cont = lastT !== null && Math.abs(t - lastT - 1 / 30) < 1e-3;\n    P = params;\n    if (!cont) for (var k = 0; k < 45; k++) model.update(1000 / 30); // settle physics after a jump in time\n    model.update(1000 / 30); app.render(); lastT = t;\n    // hand-inked outline: her silhouette, dilated\n    octx.clearRect(0, 0, outline.width, outline.height);\n    for (var a = 0; a < 12; a++) { var an = a / 12 * Math.PI * 2; octx.drawImage(app.view, PAD + Math.cos(an) * OUT, PAD + Math.sin(an) * OUT); }\n    octx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-in\"; octx.fillStyle = ink || \"#2a2433\"; octx.fillRect(0, 0, outline.width, outline.height);\n    octx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-over\";\n    sctx.clearRect(0, 0, styled.width, styled.height);\n    sctx.drawImage(outline, 0, 0); sctx.drawImage(app.view, PAD, PAD);\n    // paper grain over her, so she shares the page's texture\n    if (grain) { sctx.save(); sctx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-atop\"; sctx.globalAlpha = .28; sctx.fillStyle = sctx.createPattern(grain, \"repeat\"); sctx.fillRect(0, 0, styled.width, styled.height); sctx.restore(); }\n    return styled;\n  }\n})();\n","numLines":47,"startLine":1,"totalLines":47}},"displayPath":"demo-video\\comp\\l2d.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"196a7d46-54b5-4a53-8fd6-1180ae9b2cce","timestamp":"2026-10-12T05:17:31.081Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Computer\\\\Coding\\\\neathack\\\\SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\\\demo-video\\\\comp\\\\l2d.js\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t/* Mao, the presenter: Live2D Inc.'s official sample model \"Niziiro Mao\" (Free Material License: free for individuals and\n2\t * small teams, commercial or not; credit required). The model files are loaded at render time from Live2D's own\n3\t * repository (github.com/Live2D/CubismWebSamples) and the runtime from Live2D's CDN; they are not stored in this repo.\n4\t * Credit (video description): \"This content uses sample data owned and copyrighted by Live2D Inc. The sample data are\n5\t * utilized in accordance with terms and conditions set by Live2D Inc. This content itself is created at the author's\n6\t * sole discretion.\"\n7\t *\n8\t * window.__l2d.frame(t, params, grain, ink) renders her once per film time t with the given Live2D parameters (no random\n9\t * idle motions, no random blinks: every value comes from the film's timeline), adds a hand-inked outline and paper\n10\t * grain so she sits in the papery world, and returns that canvas. Hair and cloth physics run continuously; after a\n11\t * jump in time (the first frame of a render shard) they are settled first. */\n12\t(function () {\n13\t  \"use strict\";\n14\t  var BASE = \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Live2D/CubismWebSamples@5-r.5/Samples/Resources/\";\n15\t  var CW = 1200, CH = 2400, PAD = 24, OUT = 7;\n16\t  var app, model, im, P = {}, lastT = null, styled, sctx, outline, octx;\n17\t  window.__l2dReady = (async function () {\n18\t    app = new PIXI.Application({ width: CW, height: CH, backgroundAlpha: 0, preserveDrawingBuffer: true, autoStart: false, antialias: true });\n19\t    model = await PIXI.live2d.Live2DModel.from(BASE + \"Mao/Mao.model3.json\", { autoInteract: false, autoUpdate: false });\n20\t    im = model.internalModel;\n21\t    im.eyeBlink = undefined; im.breath = undefined; im.motionManager.update = function () { return false; };\n22\t    var sc = (CH - 40) / model.height; model.scale.set(sc); model.x = (CW - model.width) / 2; model.y = 20;\n23\t    app.stage.addChild(model);\n24\t    im.on(\"afterMotionUpdate\", function () { for (var k in P) im.coreModel.setParameterValueById(k, P[k]); });\n25\t    styled = document.createElement(\"canvas\"); styled.width = CW + 2 * PAD; styled.height = CH + 2 * PAD; sctx = styled.getContext(\"2d\");\n26\t    outline = document.createElement(\"canvas\"); outline.width = styled.width; outline.height = styled.height; octx = outline.getContext(\"2d\");\n27\t    window.__l2d = { W: styled.width, H: styled.height, top: PAD + 20, feet: PAD + CH - 20, frame: frame };\n28\t  })();\n29\t  function frame(t, params, grain, ink) {\n30\t    if (t === lastT) return styled;\n31\t    var cont = lastT !== null && Math.abs(t - lastT - 1 / 30) < 1e-3;\n32\t    P = params;\n33\t    if (!cont) for (var k = 0; k < 45; k++) model.update(1000 / 30); // settle physics after a jump in time\n34\t    model.update(1000 / 30); app.render(); lastT = t;\n35\t    // hand-inked outline: her silhouette, dilated\n36\t    octx.clearRect(0, 0, outline.width, outline.height);\n37\t    for (var a = 0; a < 12; a++) { var an = a / 12 * Math.PI * 2; octx.drawImage(app.view, PAD + Math.cos(an) * OUT, PAD + Math.sin(an) * OUT); }\n38\t    octx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-in\"; octx.fillStyle = ink || \"#2a2433\"; octx.fillRect(0, 0, outline.width, outline.height);\n39\t    octx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-over\";\n40\t    sctx.clearRect(0, 0, styled.width, styled.height);\n41\t    sctx.drawImage(outline, 0, 0); sctx.drawImage(app.view, PAD, PAD);\n42\t    // paper grain over her, so she shares the page's texture\n43\t    if (grain) { sctx.save(); sctx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-atop\"; sctx.globalAlpha = .28; sctx.fillStyle = sctx.createPattern(grain, \"repeat\"); sctx.fillRect(0, 0, styled.width, styled.height); sctx.restore(); }\n44\t    return styled;\n45\t  }\n46\t})();\n47\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Computer\\Coding\\neathack\\SpeedRadar-NeetHack","sessionId":"3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"demo-video","slug":"calm-discovering-rabbit"}
{"parentUuid":"196a7d46-54b5-4a53-8fd6-1180ae9b2cce","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\aarav\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a\\scratchpad\\apply_mao.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\aarav\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a\\scratchpad\\apply_mao.py","content":"import re, sys\ncomp, block = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\ns = open(comp, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\n\ndef rep(a, b, n=1):\n    global s\n    c = s.count(a)\n    assert c == n, f\"{c}x (want {n}): {a[:90]}\"\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n# 1) Mao replaces the old host() helper\na = s.index(\"  // host(): Sora with a timed plan of poses\")\nb = s.index(\"  function tower(g, x, base, w, h, label, lit, col) {\")\ns = s[:a] + open(block, encoding=\"utf-8\").read() + s[b:]\n\n# 2) visemes: I and U separately (Mao has a parameter per vowel)\nrep('''      if (\"ouw\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"O\";\n      if (\"eiy\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"E\";''', '''      if (\"o\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"O\";\n      if (\"uw\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"U\";\n      if (\"iy\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"I\";\n      if (c === \"e\") return \"E\";''')\n\n# 3) the real frame time, and wait for Mao before the page reports ready\nrep('''    T = t; BF = Math.floor(t * BOIL); X.setTransform(SC, 0, 0, SC, 0, 0);''', '''    T = t; TREAL = t; BF = Math.floor(t * BOIL); X.setTransform(SC, 0, 0, SC, 0, 0);''')\nrep('''  window.__ready = true;''', '''  (window.__l2dReady || Promise.resolve()).then(function () { window.__ready = true; }, function (e) { console.error(\"Live2D failed\", e); window.__ready = true; });''')\n\n# 4) Radar (the green mascot) leaves the film: Mao is the presenter now\nn0 = len(re.findall(r\"\\n\\s*radar\\(g, [^\\n]*\\);\", s))\ns = re.sub(r\"(\\n[ \\t]*)radar\\(g, [^\\n]*?\\);[ \\t]*(?=\\n)\", r\"\\1/* Mao presents here */\", s)\n# the hook's Radar burst lived inside an if-block on one line\ns = s.replace('''    if (up > 0) { /* Mao presents here */''', '''    if (false) {''')\n\n# 5) close-ups\nrep('''    var cl = lineAt(T); if (cl && cl.scene === \"hook\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 100, y: 180, w: 860 }, { size: 112 });\n  };''', '''    var cl = lineAt(T); if (cl && cl.scene === \"hook\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 100, y: 180, w: 860 }, { size: 112 });\n    // the reveal: Mao, waist-up, on focus lines\n    if (T >= l3.start - .12) closeUp(g, l3, \"#2c3260\", [C.navy2, \"#4b3f7a\", C.teal], 301, [[l3.start - .12, \"present\", \"smile\", [600, 400]], [wt(\"hook3\", [\"first\"]) - .15, \"cheer\", \"wink\"]], \"right\", wt(\"hook3\", [\"first\"]), [[wt(\"hook3\", [\"first\"]), \"sparkle\"]]);\n  };''')\ns = s.replace('''    if (cl && cl.id === \"aud1\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 0, y: 360, w: W }, { size: 130, align: \"center\" });''',\n              '''    if (cl && cl.id === \"aud1\") closeUp(g, cl, \"#f6dfcf\", [\"#f7b8a8\", \"#ffd9a0\", \"#f3a9b8\", \"#fff0d0\"], 303, [[cl.start - .1, \"present\", \"grin\"], [cl.start + cl.dur * .45, \"point\", \"wow\", [500, 400]]], \"right\", cl.start + cl.dur * .5, [[cl.start + cl.dur * .5, \"aura\"]]);''')\nrep('''    var cl = lineAt(T); if (cl && cl.scene === \"outro\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 0, y: 610, w: W }, { size: 80, align: \"center\", hold: true });''',\n    '''    var cl = lineAt(T);\n    if (cl && cl.id === \"out1\" && T < o2.start - .05) { closeUp(g, cl, \"#f6d9b8\", [\"#f7b2a0\", \"#ffd98a\", \"#f6a6c1\", \"#c4b4ee\"], 305, [[cl.start - .1, \"present\", \"smile\", [500, 400]], [wt(\"out1\", [\"source\"], .8) - .1, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], \"right\", wt(\"out1\", [\"source\"], .8), [[wt(\"out1\", [\"source\"], .8), \"sparkle\"]]); return; }\n    if (cl && cl.scene === \"outro\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 0, y: 610, w: W }, { size: 80, align: \"center\", hold: true });''')\nopen(comp, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nprint(\"radar calls removed:\", n0, \"| remaining radar(g:\", len(re.findall(r\"radar\\(g, \", s)))\n","numLines":47,"startLine":1,"totalLines":47}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\..\\Users\\aarav\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a\\scratchpad\\apply_mao.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"55e8aa37-29c3-488c-80bc-a2c7602a55cd","timestamp":"2026-10-12T05:17:31.081Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\aarav\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a\\\\scratchpad\\\\apply_mao.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport re, sys\n2\tcomp, block = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\n3\ts = open(comp, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\n4\t\n5\tdef rep(a, b, n=1):\n6\t    global s\n7\t    c = s.count(a)\n8\t    assert c == n, f\"{c}x (want {n}): {a[:90]}\"\n9\t    s = s.replace(a, b)\n10\t\n11\t# 1) Mao replaces the old host() helper\n12\ta = s.index(\"  // host(): Sora with a timed plan of poses\")\n13\tb = s.index(\"  function tower(g, x, base, w, h, label, lit, col) {\")\n14\ts = s[:a] + open(block, encoding=\"utf-8\").read() + s[b:]\n15\t\n16\t# 2) visemes: I and U separately (Mao has a parameter per vowel)\n17\trep('''      if (\"ouw\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"O\";\n18\t      if (\"eiy\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"E\";''', '''      if (\"o\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"O\";\n19\t      if (\"uw\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"U\";\n20\t      if (\"iy\".indexOf(c) >= 0) return \"I\";\n21\t      if (c === \"e\") return \"E\";''')\n22\t\n23\t# 3) the real frame time, and wait for Mao before the page reports ready\n24\trep('''    T = t; BF = Math.floor(t * BOIL); X.setTransform(SC, 0, 0, SC, 0, 0);''', '''    T = t; TREAL = t; BF = Math.floor(t * BOIL); X.setTransform(SC, 0, 0, SC, 0, 0);''')\n25\trep('''  window.__ready = true;''', '''  (window.__l2dReady || Promise.resolve()).then(function () { window.__ready = true; }, function (e) { console.error(\"Live2D failed\", e); window.__ready = true; });''')\n26\t\n27\t# 4) Radar (the green mascot) leaves the film: Mao is the presenter now\n28\tn0 = len(re.findall(r\"\\n\\s*radar\\(g, [^\\n]*\\);\", s))\n29\ts = re.sub(r\"(\\n[ \\t]*)radar\\(g, [^\\n]*?\\);[ \\t]*(?=\\n)\", r\"\\1/* Mao presents here */\", s)\n30\t# the hook's Radar burst lived inside an if-block on one line\n31\ts = s.replace('''    if (up > 0) { /* Mao presents here */''', '''    if (false) {''')\n32\t\n33\t# 5) close-ups\n34\trep('''    var cl = lineAt(T); if (cl && cl.scene === \"hook\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 100, y: 180, w: 860 }, { size: 112 });\n35\t  };''', '''    var cl = lineAt(T); if (cl && cl.scene === \"hook\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 100, y: 180, w: 860 }, { size: 112 });\n36\t    // the reveal: Mao, waist-up, on focus lines\n37\t    if (T >= l3.start - .12) closeUp(g, l3, \"#2c3260\", [C.navy2, \"#4b3f7a\", C.teal], 301, [[l3.start - .12, \"present\", \"smile\", [600, 400]], [wt(\"hook3\", [\"first\"]) - .15, \"cheer\", \"wink\"]], \"right\", wt(\"hook3\", [\"first\"]), [[wt(\"hook3\", [\"first\"]), \"sparkle\"]]);\n38\t  };''')\n39\ts = s.replace('''    if (cl && cl.id === \"aud1\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 0, y: 360, w: W }, { size: 130, align: \"center\" });''',\n40\t              '''    if (cl && cl.id === \"aud1\") closeUp(g, cl, \"#f6dfcf\", [\"#f7b8a8\", \"#ffd9a0\", \"#f3a9b8\", \"#fff0d0\"], 303, [[cl.start - .1, \"present\", \"grin\"], [cl.start + cl.dur * .45, \"point\", \"wow\", [500, 400]]], \"right\", cl.start + cl.dur * .5, [[cl.start + cl.dur * .5, \"aura\"]]);''')\n41\trep('''    var cl = lineAt(T); if (cl && cl.scene === \"outro\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 0, y: 610, w: W }, { size: 80, align: \"center\", hold: true });''',\n42\t    '''    var cl = lineAt(T);\n43\t    if (cl && cl.id === \"out1\" && T < o2.start - .05) { closeUp(g, cl, \"#f6d9b8\", [\"#f7b2a0\", \"#ffd98a\", \"#f6a6c1\", \"#c4b4ee\"], 305, [[cl.start - .1, \"present\", \"smile\", [500, 400]], [wt(\"out1\", [\"source\"], .8) - .1, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], \"right\", wt(\"out1\", [\"source\"], .8), [[wt(\"out1\", [\"source\"], .8), \"sparkle\"]]); return; }\n44\t    if (cl && cl.scene === \"outro\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 0, y: 610, w: W }, { size: 80, align: \"center\", hold: true });''')\n45\topen(comp, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\n46\tprint(\"radar calls removed:\", n0, \"| remaining radar(g:\", len(re.findall(r\"radar\\(g, \", s)))\n47\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Computer\\Coding\\neathack\\SpeedRadar-NeetHack","sessionId":"3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"demo-video","slug":"calm-discovering-rabbit"}
{"parentUuid":"55e8aa37-29c3-488c-80bc-a2c7602a55cd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\aarav\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a\\scratchpad\\mao_block.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\aarav\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a\\scratchpad\\mao_block.js","content":"  // ── Mao (Live2D, see l2d.js): poses → Live2D parameters, drawn with her feet at (x, y) and h units tall ──\n  var TREAL = 0; // the frame being rendered (wipes redraw the old scene at a frozen T; Mao always uses the real frame)\n  var VOW = { A: \"ParamA\", E: \"ParamE\", I: \"ParamI\", O: \"ParamO\", U: \"ParamU\" };\n  function maoPose(pose, expr, look, talk, vis, t) {\n    var P = { ParamA: 0, ParamI: 0, ParamU: 0, ParamE: 0, ParamO: 0, ParamEyeLSmile: 0, ParamEyeRSmile: 0, ParamCheek: .25,\n      ParamBrowLY: 0, ParamBrowRY: 0, ParamBrowLAngle: 0, ParamBrowRAngle: 0, ParamEyeBallY: 0,\n      ParamArmRA01: 0, ParamArmRA02: 0, ParamArmRA03: 0, ParamArmLA01: 0, ParamArmLA02: 0, ParamArmLA03: 0, ParamWandRotate: 0 };\n    var op = Math.min(1, talk * 1.3);\n    if (op > .05 && VOW[vis]) P[VOW[vis]] = op;\n    var blink = ((t * .9) % 3.1) < .12 ? 0 : 1;\n    P.ParamEyeLOpen = P.ParamEyeROpen = blink;\n    if (expr === \"grin\") { P.ParamEyeLSmile = P.ParamEyeRSmile = 1; P.ParamCheek = 1; }\n    if (expr === \"wink\") { P.ParamEyeROpen = 0; P.ParamEyeRSmile = 1; P.ParamCheek = .8; }\n    if (expr === \"wow\") { P.ParamEyeLOpen = P.ParamEyeROpen = 1.2 * blink; P.ParamBrowLY = P.ParamBrowRY = 1; if (op < .25) P.ParamO = .55; }\n    if (expr === \"think\") { P.ParamBrowLAngle = -.7; P.ParamBrowRAngle = .4; P.ParamEyeBallY = .6; }\n    // head and body: idle sway, nods while she talks, turn toward what she is presenting\n    P.ParamAngleX = look * 22 + Math.sin(t * .9) * 4;\n    P.ParamAngleY = Math.sin(t * 1.3) * 3 + (talk > .15 ? Math.sin(t * 7) * 5 * talk : 0) + (expr === \"think\" ? 8 : 0);\n    P.ParamAngleZ = Math.sin(t * .7) * 5 + (expr === \"think\" ? 9 : 0);\n    P.ParamBodyAngleX = Math.sin(t * .8) * 3 + look * 5;\n    P.ParamBodyAngleZ = Math.sin(t * .6) * 2;\n    P.ParamBreath = (Math.sin(t * 2.2) + 1) / 2;\n    P.ParamEyeBallX = look * .7;\n    // arms (her wand is the pointer)\n    if (pose === \"point\") { P.ParamArmRA01 = 30; P.ParamArmLA01 = 30; P.ParamArmLA02 = -20; }\n    else if (pose === \"present\") { P.ParamArmRA01 = 17; P.ParamWandRotate = 3; }\n    else if (pose === \"think\") { P.ParamArmLA01 = 30; P.ParamArmLA02 = -20; P.ParamArmRA01 = 30; P.ParamArmRA02 = -20; P.ParamArmRA03 = 30; }\n    else if (pose === \"cheer\") { P.ParamArmRA01 = 26; P.ParamWandRotate = 10; P.ParamArmLA01 = 30; P.ParamArmLA02 = -20; }\n    else if (pose === \"wave\") { P.ParamArmRA01 = 22 + Math.sin(t * 9) * 6; P.ParamWandRotate = 6 + Math.sin(t * 9) * 4; }\n    return P;\n  }\n  function blendP(a, b, k) { var o = {}; for (var key in b) o[key] = a[key] == null ? b[key] : a[key] + (b[key] - a[key]) * k; return o; }\n  // plan = [[t, pose, expr, at], ...]; poses blend over .3 s; o.fx = [[t, \"sparkle\"|\"aura\"], ...]\n  function maoAt(plan, x, flip) {\n    var ci = 0; for (var i = 0; i < plan.length; i++) if (TREAL >= plan[i][0]) ci = i;\n    var cur = plan[ci], prev = plan[Math.max(0, ci - 1)], k = ci === 0 ? 1 : eOut(prog(TREAL, cur[0], .3));\n    var talk = envAt(TREAL), vis = viseme(TREAL);\n    function lk(p) { var at = p[3]; if (!at) return 0; return clamp((at[0] - x) / 700, -1, 1) * (flip ? -1 : 1) * -1; }\n    return blendP(maoPose(prev[1], prev[2], lk(prev), talk, vis, TREAL), maoPose(cur[1], cur[2], lk(cur), talk, vis, TREAL), k);\n  }\n  function maoFx(P, fx) {\n    (fx || []).forEach(function (f) {\n      var d = TREAL - f[0]; if (d < 0 || d > 1.6) return;\n      if (f[1] === \"sparkle\") { P.ParamHeartLightOn = 1; P.ParamHeartLight = d / 1.6 * 30; P.ParamWandInk = 1; }\n      if (f[1] === \"aura\") { P.ParamAuraOn = 1; P.ParamAura = d / 1.6 * 30; }\n    });\n    return P;\n  }\n  function maoImg(P) { return window.__l2d ? window.__l2d.frame(TREAL, P, grain, C.ink) : null; }\n  // full body, feet at (x, y), h units tall; flip mirrors her so she faces/points to the right\n  function maoDraw(g, img, x, y, h, flip, hop) {\n    if (!img) return; var L = window.__l2d, sc = h / (L.feet - L.top);\n    g.save(); g.translate(x, y + (hop || 0)); g.scale(flip ? -sc : sc, sc);\n    g.fillStyle = C.shadow; g.beginPath(); g.ellipse(0, 0, L.W * .22, 40, 0, 0, TAU); g.fill();\n    g.drawImage(img, -L.W / 2, -L.feet);\n    g.restore();\n    if (CHK && g === X) chkRect(\"char\", g, x - h * .26, y - h, h * .52, h, \"mao\");\n  }\n  // host(): same plan format the scenes already use (Sora's API); s = old scale → height\n  function host(g, x, y, s, plan, o) {\n    o = o || {}; var flip = o.face !== -1;\n    if (CHK && g === X) CHKLOG.push({ kind: \"charStart\" });\n    var P = maoFx(maoAt(plan, x, flip), o.fx);\n    maoDraw(g, maoImg(P), x + (o.walk ? 0 : 0), y, s * 600, flip, hopY(o.hop, 60));\n  }\n  // ── anime close-up: waist-up shot on focus lines; camera pushes in, punches on the key word ──\n  function focusLines(g, cx, cy, col, intensity, seed) {\n    g.save(); g.translate(cx, cy);\n    var n = 90, f = Math.floor(T * 12);\n    for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      var a = (i + hash(i * 3.7 + seed) * .8) / n * TAU, r0 = 330 + hash(i * 9.1 + f * .37) * 260, len = 900 + hash(i * 1.3 + f) * 600;\n      var w = (3 + hash(i * 5.3 + f * .11) * 14) * intensity;\n      g.fillStyle = col; g.beginPath();\n      g.moveTo(Math.cos(a) * r0, Math.sin(a) * r0);\n      g.lineTo(Math.cos(a + w / r0 / 2) * (r0 + len), Math.sin(a + w / r0 / 2) * (r0 + len));\n      g.lineTo(Math.cos(a - w / r0 / 2) * (r0 + len), Math.sin(a - w / r0 / 2) * (r0 + len));\n      g.fill();\n    }\n    g.restore();\n  }\n  // line: the narration line; plan: Mao's poses; side: \"right\" (she is on the right, words on the left) or \"left\"\n  function closeUp(g, line, base, blots, seed, plan, side, punchAt, fx) {\n    g.drawImage(paper(\"cu\" + seed, base, blots, seed), 0, 0);\n    var right = side !== \"left\", fcx = right ? 1360 : 560;\n    var punch = punchAt == null ? 0 : Math.exp(-Math.max(0, T - punchAt) * 9) * (T >= punchAt ? 1 : 0);\n    focusLines(g, fcx, 470, \"rgba(255,250,240,.55)\", 1 + punch * 1.5, seed);\n    var P = maoFx(maoAt(plan, fcx, !right), fx), img = maoImg(P), L = window.__l2d;\n    var push = 1 + prog(T, line.start - .3, line.dur + .6) * .06 + punch * .07, tilt = (right ? -1 : 1) * (.03 + punch * .02);\n    if (img) {\n      // waist-up crop: top 58% of her figure, scaled so the crop fills the frame height\n      var cropH = (L.feet - L.top) * .58, sc = 1240 / cropH * push;\n      g.save(); g.translate(fcx, 1080 + 40); g.rotate(tilt); g.scale(right ? sc : -sc, sc);\n      g.drawImage(img, -L.W / 2, -(L.top + cropH) - 30);\n      g.restore();\n    }\n    if (punch > .05) { g.save(); g.globalAlpha = punch * .55; g.fillStyle = C.white; g.fillRect(0, 0, W, H); g.restore(); }\n    bigLine(g, line, { x: right ? 90 : 1000, y: 260, w: 830 }, { size: 108, hold: false });\n  }\n","numLines":99,"startLine":1,"totalLines":99}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\..\\Users\\aarav\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a\\scratchpad\\mao_block.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d6e7a33a-a7ba-49e0-92cf-bf3af1913db5","timestamp":"2026-10-12T05:17:31.081Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\aarav\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\c--Computer-Coding-neathack-SpeedRadar-NeetHack\\\\3ac9aaf8-f1d5-4ab4-b5ac-62a9bdcabd6a\\\\scratchpad\\\\mao_block.js\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t  // ── Mao (Liv