{"parentUuid":"fc1a7d8a-6304-4a48-ab01-bb89d40067b5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a0bef22b-6359-4917-a7d2-c51ff20cff84","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018zyGpDnwqiHPqqtQkyxogk","type":"tool_result","content":"hook1 | So... your competitor just doubled their em ell team. | \r\nhook2 | And you? You'll find out next quarter. | \r\nhook3 | Unless your agent finds out first. | \r\ntitle1 | This is Spend Radar. It reads your books, checks the market, and then, before it tells you anything, it tries to prove itself wrong. | \r\nrun1 | Let's watch it work, on a real run. | runs/1011-777bb7 (data mode: real)\r\nrun2 | First, the model writes a plan. Then the agent works through it, one tool call at a time. | runs/1011-777bb7/state.json plan_rationale, done (41)\r\nrun3 | It reads the budget, the invoices and the policy, then pulls real competitor headcount from Crust-data. | state.json done; competitors (5)\r\nrun4 | Python checks every single result. Seventy-one checks in all. And here's one that fails: a budget row that doesn't add up. | state.json checks (71); decisions[t01] 1.45% off\r\nrun5 | The rule says, just mark it low confidence. But the model decides to re-read that exact row instead. | decisions[t01]: default mark_low_confidence, chosen narrow_range\r\nrun6 | A scanned PDF gets read another way. A corrupt one gets flagged, and the run keeps going. | decisions t15 reparse_alt; t16/t16r reparse_alt, skip; not_analysed\r\nrun7 | In this run, five of its ten recovery calls beat the default rule. | run 1011-777bb7 metrics recovery_non_default 5 / recovery_decisions 10\r\naud1 | Now, here's our favourite part. | \r\naud2 | The agent flagged a gap of up to five point two eight million dollars in Acme's em ell team. | run 1011-777bb7 finding f_ml_ai\r\naud3 | Then it argued with itself, and overturned its own claim. | \r\naud4 | So that wrong number never reaches the report. | \r\ngen1 | We tested it on seven companies. Six of them, it had never seen before. | summary.companies 7, held_out_companies 6\r\ngen2 | Every planted error was caught, with zero false alarms. | summary.latest_runs_all_caught 7, latest_runs_false_alarms 0\r\nnl1 | We found and fixed our bugs in neet logs. | \r\nnl2 | In five runs before one fix, the agent threw away three of its five competitors, every time. After the fix, it kept all five, every time. | evidence/case-studies/02-competitor-substitution.md, rerun n = 5 per side\r\nnl3 | Another showed the same data getting three different verdicts. Now, it gets one, every time. | evidence/case-studies/05-audit-verdict-variance.md\r\nnl4 | Then we tried twenty-four real, public invoices. The reader was copying the net amount instead of the total. After the fix, zero silent wrong totals. | evidence/case-studies/06-real-invoices-gross-vs-net.md (12 tuned-on + 12 held-out, n = 3 passes: 2 and 4 per pass -> 0)\r\nent1 | Entire gave our coding agent a memory. More than ninety checkpoints, each one linking a commit to its prompt. | evidence/frontend_data.json entire.checkpoints (91 on 12 Oct)\r\nent2 | So you can start from any trace, and follow it back to the code, the commit, and the exact prompt that wrote it. | evidence/explain/5fcef2f7f2f8-decide-recovery.md\r\nent3 | Six review trails later, Entire's runners have caught four real bugs, and we fixed every one. | evidence/frontend_data.json entire.trails: 6 trails, 4 findings, all resolved (a16758f, 62c6b69, bd079ca)\r\ncfo1 | Then, CFO dot AI turned our measured costs into a business plan. | \r\ncfo2 | The AI costs under three cents a run. Competitor data is about ninety-nine percent of the cost. | cfo.ai Assumptions: LLM cost per run $0.0285; judge summary: Crustdata ~99% of COGS\r\ncfo3 | Across seven scenarios, the base case turns cash-flow positive in January twenty twenty-eight. Even paying for a human to review flagged invoices, it still does. | frontend_data.json business.cfoai_model: Base first positive 2028-01; Managed review 2028-01 (month 15)\r\nout1 | Spend Radar. Every number has a source. | \r\nout2 | From team kwep. Hashtag neet hack! | \r\n      txt(g, c.name.replace(\" Inc.\", \"\"), -106, -84, 30, { fill: C.ink }); txt(g, c.industry, -106, -50, 22, { fill: \"#6a6170\", weight: 500 });\n      if (c.role === \"held_out\" && T > six - .1) { var hk = eBack(prog(T, six + i * .05, .3)); g.save(); g.translate(120, -150); g.rotate(.12); g.scale(hk, hk); inkRR(g, -80, -22, 160, 44, 10, C.indigo, 4); txt(g, \"HELD-OUT\", 0, 12, 24, { align: \"center\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.ink }); g.restore(); }\n      var L2 = c.latest || {};\n      for (var p = 0; p < (L2.total || 0); p++) {\n        var sk = eBack(prog(T, caught - .2 + i * .08 + p * .04, .3));\n        inkRR(g, -170 + p * 58, -6, 48, 48, 10, sk > 0 ? C.green : \"rgba(0,0,0,.08)\", 4);\n        if (sk > 0) { g.save(); g.translate(-146 + p * 58, 18); g.scale(sk, sk); inkPath(g, [[-11, 0], [-3, 9], [12, -10]], false, null, C.white, 6); g.restore(); }\n      }\n      txt(g, L2.caught + \" / \" + L2.total, 170, 110, 44, { align: \"right\", fill: T > caught + .3 ? C.mintD : \"#9a92a0\" });\n      g.restore();\n    });\n    stamp(g, \"0 FALSE ALARMS\", 1180, 690, wt(\"gen2\", [\"zero\", \"0\"], .7), C.mintD, 54, .06);\n    host(g, 1790, 1075, 0.8, [[g1.start, \"present\", \"smile\"], [caught - .1, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], { face: -1, hop: caught });\n    confetti(g, 960, 380, caught);\n    /* Mao presents here */\n    var cl = lineAt(T);\n    if (cl && cl.id === \"gen2\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 380, y: 800, w: 980 }, { size: 68 }); else caption(g, sc, null);\n  };\n\n  // 06 NEATLOGS — real span waterfall, magnifier on case study 02, the 3 → 1 verdict dice (case study 05)\n  S.neatlogs = function (g, sc) {\n    var n1 = L(\"nl1\"), n2 = L(\"nl2\"), n3 = L(\"nl3\"), n4 = L(\"nl4\");\n    g.drawImage(paper(\"nl\", \"#1f2440\", [\"#2c3260\", \"#3b2f5a\", \"#22364f\", \"#2f4a5c\"], 97), 0, 0);\n    txt(g, \"neatlogs\", 110, 150, 92, { fill: C.cream, stroke: C.ink, sw: 12 });\n    if (n4 && T >= n4.start - .05) { // real public invoices: the reader copied the net amount (case study 06)\n      var ri = FX.real_invoices || {}, ex = ri.example || {}, sw = ri.silent_wrong_per_pass || {};\n      txt(g, (ri.n_invoices || 24) + \" real public invoices (FCC broadcast ads) · case study 06\", 115, 200, 28, { font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: \"#a8aac4\" });\n      var netT = wt(\"nl4\", [\"net\"], .45), fixT = wt(\"nl4\", [\"fix\"], .75), zeroT = wt(\"nl4\", [\"zero\", \"0\"], .85);\n      var pk = eBack(prog(T, n4.start, .45));\n      g.save(); g.translate(560, 590); g.rotate(-.04); g.scale(pk, pk);\n      inkRR(g, -330, -330, 660, 660, 12, C.white, 6);\n      txt(g, \"INVOICE\", -290, -260, 44, { font: COMIC, weight: 400, fill: C.ink, ls: 3 });\n      for (var r = 0; r < 5; r++) { inkLine(g, -290, -190 + r * 46, 150, -190 + r * 46, 3, \"rgba(42,36,51,.3)\"); }\n      var fixed = T > fixT, pickNet = T > netT && !fixed;\n      inkRR(g, -300, 60, 600, 80, 10, fixed ? \"#d6f1dc\" : \"#fff\", 4, fixed ? C.mintD : C.ink);\n      txt(g, \"TOTAL\", -270, 115, 40, { fill: C.ink }); txt(g, \"$\" + (ex.total || \"\"), 270, 115, 44, { align: \"right\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.ink });\n      inkRR(g, -300, 170, 600, 80, 10, pickNet ? \"#ffd9d6\" : \"#fff\", 4, pickNet ? C.red : C.ink);\n      txt(g, \"NET AMOUNT DUE\", -270, 225, 34, { fill: C.ink }); txt(g, \"$\" + (ex.net_read || \"\"), 270, 225, 44, { align: \"right\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.ink });\n      g.restore();\n      if (pickNet) { stamp(g, \"READ THE NET ✗\", 560, 520, netT + .2, C.red, 56, -.08); }\n      if (fixed) { stamp(g, \"READS THE TOTAL ✓\", 560, 520, fixT, C.mintD, 56, -.08); }\n      // the count of silent wrong totals per pass, before -> after\n      var zk = eBack(prog(T, zeroT - .3, .4));\n      if (zk > 0) {\n        g.save(); g.translate(1330, 520); g.scale(zk, zk);\n        inkRR(g, -360, -220, 720, 440, 24, C.cream, 6);\n        txt(g, \"silent wrong totals, per pass\", 0, -150, 32, { align: \"center\", fill: C.ink, weight: 700 });\n        txt(g, \"tuned-on 12:\", -320, -60, 34, { fill: C.ink, weight: 600 }); txt(g, sw.tuned_v1 + \"  →  \" + sw.tuned_v2, 320, -60, 46, { align: \"right\", fill: C.mintD });\n        txt(g, \"held-out 12:\", -320, 30, 34, { fill: C.ink, weight: 600 }); txt(g, sw.heldout_v1 + \"  →  \" + sw.heldout_v2, 320, 30, 46, { align: \"right\", fill: C.mintD });\n        txt(g, \"n = 3 passes each\", 0, 150, 26, { align: \"center\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: \"#6a6170\" });\n        g.restore();\n      }\n      sfxWord(g, \"OOPS!\", 900, 250, netT + .1, 100, C.red, -.1);\n      sfxWord(g, \"FIXED!\", 1620, 230, zeroT, 100, C.green, .1);\n      host(g, 1790, 1075, .75, [[n4.start, \"present\", \"smile\"], [netT - .1, \"point\", \"wow\", [560, 640]], [zeroT - .1, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], { face: -1, hop: zeroT });\n      confetti(g, 1330, 420, zeroT);\n      caption(g, sc, null);\n      return;\n    }\n    if (T < n3.start - .05) {\n      txt(g, \"case study 02 · rerun: 5 runs per side, same models and data\", 115, 200, 28, { font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: \"#a8aac4\" });\n      var spans = [[\"plan\", 0, .1], [\"act:read_budget\", .1, .06], [\"verify:totals\", .16, .03], [\"act:fetch_competitor\", .2, .1], [\"decide:recovery\", .3, .05, 1], [\"act:fetch_jobs\", .35, .08],\n        [\"decide:recovery\", .43, .05, 1], [\"act:classify_titles\", .48, .12], [\"decide:recovery\", .6, .05, 1], [\"audit:f_ml_ai\", .72, .1], [\"report\", .86, .1]];\n      spans.forEach(function (s, i) {\n        var y = 260 + i * 50, k = prog(T, n1.start + .1 + i * .07, .35), x0 = 560 + s[1] * 1150, w = s[2] * 1150 * eOut(k);\n        if (k <= 0) return;\n        txt(g, s[0], 520, y + 28, 26, { align: \"right\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: s[3] ? C.yellow : \"#cfd0e6\" });\n        inkRR(g, x0, y + 6, Math.max(8, w), 30, 8, s[3] ? C.orange : C.teal2, 3);\n      });\n      var three = wt(\"nl2\", [\"three\", \"3\"], .2), fix = wt(\"nl2\", [\"fix\"], .45), cut = wt(\"nl2\", [\"kept\"], .75);\n      if (T > n2.start) {\n        var mk = eOut(prog(T, n2.start, .4));\n        g.save(); g.globalAlpha = mk; inkCircle(g, 1440, 560, 230, \"rgba(20,24,48,.94)\", 8);\n        if (T < fix) {\n          txt(g, \"substitute_competitor\", 1440, 450, 27, { align: \"center\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.orange });\n          [\"Honeycomb\", \"Arize\", \"Chronosphere\"].forEach(function (nm, i) { var fly = prog(T, three + .2 + i * .2, .5); txt(g, \"✗ \" + nm, 1440 + fly * 260 * (i - 1), 520 + i * 56 - fly * 160, 38, { align: \"center\", fill: C.red, weight: 700 }); });\n          txt(g, \"→ New Relic (3,095)\", 1440, 700, 30, { align: \"center\", fill: C.cream, weight: 600 }); txt(g, \"→ Datadog (10,482)\", 1440, 740, 30, { align: \"center\", fill: C.cream, weight: 600 });\n        } else {\n          (RUN.competitors || []).forEach(function (c, i) { txt(g, \"✓ \" + c.name, 1440, 430 + i * 50, 34, { align: \"center\", fill: C.green, weight: 700 }); });\n          var c2 = FX.case02 || {};\n          txt(g, \"5 of 5 kept\", 1440, 700, 42, { align: \"center\", fill: C.yellow, weight: 700 });\n          txt(g, \"in \" + (c2.runs_per_side || 5) + \" of \" + (c2.runs_per_side || 5) + \" runs\", 1440, 745, 32, { align: \"center\", fill: C.cream, weight: 600 });\n        }\n        g.restore(); inkLine(g, 1600, 720, 1660, 790, 22, C.ink);\n        sfxWord(g, \"YOINK!\", 1220, 300, three + .4, 100, C.orange, -.12);\n        sfxWord(g, \"FIXED!\", 1700, 250, fix + .2, 100, C.green, .1);\n      }\n      /* Mao presents here */\n      host(g, 1790, 1075, 0.8, [[n1.start, \"present\", \"smile\"], [n2.start, \"point\", \"smile\", [1440, 560]], [fix, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], { face: -1, hop: fix });\n    } else {\n      txt(g, \"case study 05 · same Acme data · 5 identical runs per side\", 115, 200, 28, { font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: \"#a8aac4\" });\n      var one = wt(\"nl3\", [\"one\", \"1\"], .8), before = (FX.case05 || {}).before || [], after = (FX.case05 || {}).after || [];\n      var COL = { confirmed: C.green, overturned: C.red, downgraded: C.yellow };\n      before.forEach(function (v, i) {\n        var land = T > one + i * .08, spin = land ? eBack(prog(T, one + i * .08, .4)) : 0, cur = land ? after[i] : v;\n        var k = eBack(prog(T, n3.start + i * .1, .4)); if (k <= 0) return;\n        g.save(); g.translate(300 + i * 300, 560 + (land ? 0 : Math.sin(T * 9 + i) * 14)); g.scale(k, k); g.rotate(land ? (1 - spin) * TAU : Math.sin(T * 6 + i) * .15);\n        inkRR(g, -125, -125, 250, 250, 30, COL[cur] || C.cream, 6);\n        txt(g, \"run \" + (i + 1), 0, -70, 26, { align: \"center\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.ink }); txt(g, cur, 0, 20, 36, { align: \"center\", fill: C.ink, weight: 700 });\n        g.restore();\n      });\n      var big = T < one ? \"3 verdicts\" : \"1 verdict\";\n      txt(g, big, 960, 870, 110, { align: \"center\", font: COMIC, weight: 400, fill: T < one ? C.red : C.yellow, stroke: C.ink, sw: 14, ls: 4 });\n      sfxWord(g, \"CLICK!\", 1650, 300, one, 100, C.yellow, .1);\n      host(g, 1790, 1075, 0.8, [[n3.start, \"think\", \"think\"], [one - .1, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], { face: -1, hop: one });\n    }\n    caption(g, sc, null);\n  };\n\n  // 07 ENTIRE — commits fall in with checkpoint stickers; a detective board traces span → code → commit → prompt; runner-bots catch 2 bugs\n  S.entire = function (g, sc) {\n    var e1 = L(\"ent1\"), e2 = L(\"ent2\"), e3 = L(\"ent3\"), X2 = FX.explain || {};\n    g.drawImage(paper(\"ent\", \"#dcd1f3\", [\"#c4b4ee\", \"#efe6ff\", \"#b6c8f0\", \"#f3d9ef\"], 113), 0, 0);\n    txt(g, \"Entire\", 110, 160, 92, { fill: C.ink });\n    if (T < e2.start - .05) {\n      (FX.commits || []).slice(0, 6).forEach(function (c, i) {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"62b661ac-493b-47d2-bf1d-6a199447a20d","timestamp":"2026-10-12T05:17:41.109Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"hook1 | So... your competitor just doubled their em ell team. | \r\nhook2 | And you? You'll find out next quarter. | \r\nhook3 | Unless your agent finds out first. | \r\ntitle1 | This is Spend Radar. It reads your books, checks the market, and then, before it tells you anything, it tries to prove itself wrong. | \r\nrun1 | Let's watch it work, on a real run. | runs/1011-777bb7 (data mode: real)\r\nrun2 | First, the model writes a plan. Then the agent works through it, one tool call at a time. | runs/1011-777bb7/state.json plan_rationale, done (41)\r\nrun3 | It reads the budget, the invoices and the policy, then pulls real competitor headcount from Crust-data. | state.json done; competitors (5)\r\nrun4 | Python checks every single result. Seventy-one checks in all. And here's one that fails: a budget row that doesn't add up. | state.json checks (71); decisions[t01] 1.45% off\r\nrun5 | The rule says, just mark it low confidence. But the model decides to re-read that exact row instead. | decisions[t01]: default mark_low_confidence, chosen narrow_range\r\nrun6 | A scanned PDF gets read another way. A corrupt one gets flagged, and the run keeps going. | decisions t15 reparse_alt; t16/t16r reparse_alt, skip; not_analysed\r\nrun7 | In this run, five of its ten recovery calls beat the default rule. | run 1011-777bb7 metrics recovery_non_default 5 / recovery_decisions 10\r\naud1 | Now, here's our favourite part. | \r\naud2 | The agent flagged a gap of up to five point two eight million dollars in Acme's em ell team. | run 1011-777bb7 finding f_ml_ai\r\naud3 | Then it argued with itself, and overturned its own claim. | \r\naud4 | So that wrong number never reaches the report. | \r\ngen1 | We tested it on seven companies. Six of them, it had never seen before. | summary.companies 7, held_out_companies 6\r\ngen2 | Every planted error was caught, with zero false alarms. | summary.latest_runs_all_caught 7, latest_runs_false_alarms 0\r\nnl1 | We found and fixed our bugs in neet logs. | \r\nnl2 | In five runs before one fix, the agent threw away three of its five competitors, every time. After the fix, it kept all five, every time. | evidence/case-studies/02-competitor-substitution.md, rerun n = 5 per side\r\nnl3 | Another showed the same data getting three different verdicts. Now, it gets one, every time. | evidence/case-studies/05-audit-verdict-variance.md\r\nnl4 | Then we tried twenty-four real, public invoices. The reader was copying the net amount instead of the total. After the fix, zero silent wrong totals. | evidence/case-studies/06-real-invoices-gross-vs-net.md (12 tuned-on + 12 held-out, n = 3 passes: 2 and 4 per pass -> 0)\r\nent1 | Entire gave our coding agent a memory. More than ninety checkpoints, each one linking a commit to its prompt. | evidence/frontend_data.json entire.checkpoints (91 on 12 Oct)\r\nent2 | So you can start from any trace, and follow it back to the code, the commit, and the exact prompt that wrote it. | evidence/explain/5fcef2f7f2f8-decide-recovery.md\r\nent3 | Six review trails later, Entire's runners have caught four real bugs, and we fixed every one. | evidence/frontend_data.json entire.trails: 6 trails, 4 findings, all resolved (a16758f, 62c6b69, bd079ca)\r\ncfo1 | Then, CFO dot AI turned our measured costs into a business plan. | \r\ncfo2 | The AI costs under three cents a run. Competitor data is about ninety-nine percent of the cost. | cfo.ai Assumptions: LLM cost per run $0.0285; judge summary: Crustdata ~99% of COGS\r\ncfo3 | Across seven scenarios, the base case turns cash-flow positive in January twenty twenty-eight. Even paying for a human to review flagged invoices, it still does. | frontend_data.json business.cfoai_model: Base first positive 2028-01; Managed review 2028-01 (month 15)\r\nout1 | Spend Radar. Every number has a source. | \r\nout2 | From team kwep. Hashtag neet hack! | \r\n      txt(g, c.name.replace(\" Inc.\", \"\"), -106, -84, 30, { fill: C.ink }); txt(g, c.industry, -106, -50, 22, { fill: \"#6a6170\", weight: 500 });\n      if (c.role === \"held_out\" && T > six - .1) { var hk = eBack(prog(T, six + i * .05, .3)); g.save(); g.translate(120, -150); g.rotate(.12); g.scale(hk, hk); inkRR(g, -80, -22, 160, 44, 10, C.indigo, 4); txt(g, \"HELD-OUT\", 0, 12, 24, { align: \"center\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.ink }); g.restore(); }\n      var L2 = c.latest || {};\n      for (var p = 0; p < (L2.total || 0); p++) {\n        var sk = eBack(prog(T, caught - .2 + i * .08 + p * .04, .3));\n        inkRR(g, -170 + p * 58, -6, 48, 48, 10, sk > 0 ? C.green : \"rgba(0,0,0,.08)\", 4);\n        if (sk > 0) { g.save(); g.translate(-146 + p * 58, 18); g.scale(sk, sk); inkPath(g, [[-11, 0], [-3, 9], [12, -10]], false, null, C.white, 6); g.restore(); }\n      }\n      txt(g, L2.caught + \" / \" + L2.total, 170, 110, 44, { align: \"right\", fill: T > caught + .3 ? C.mintD : \"#9a92a0\" });\n      g.restore();\n    });\n    stamp(g, \"0 FALSE ALARMS\", 1180, 690, wt(\"gen2\", [\"zero\", \"0\"], .7), C.mintD, 54, .06);\n    host(g, 1790, 1075, 0.8, [[g1.start, \"present\", \"smile\"], [caught - .1, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], { face: -1, hop: caught });\n    confetti(g, 960, 380, caught);\n    /* Mao presents here */\n    var cl = lineAt(T);\n    if (cl && cl.id === \"gen2\") bigLine(g, cl, { x: 380, y: 800, w: 980 }, { size: 68 }); else caption(g, sc, null);\n  };\n\n  // 06 NEATLOGS — real span waterfall, magnifier on case study 02, the 3 → 1 verdict dice (case study 05)\n  S.neatlogs = function (g, sc) {\n    var n1 = L(\"nl1\"), n2 = L(\"nl2\"), n3 = L(\"nl3\"), n4 = L(\"nl4\");\n    g.drawImage(paper(\"nl\", \"#1f2440\", [\"#2c3260\", \"#3b2f5a\", \"#22364f\", \"#2f4a5c\"], 97), 0, 0);\n    txt(g, \"neatlogs\", 110, 150, 92, { fill: C.cream, stroke: C.ink, sw: 12 });\n    if (n4 && T >= n4.start - .05) { // real public invoices: the reader copied the net amount (case study 06)\n      var ri = FX.real_invoices || {}, ex = ri.example || {}, sw = ri.silent_wrong_per_pass || {};\n      txt(g, (ri.n_invoices || 24) + \" real public invoices (FCC broadcast ads) · case study 06\", 115, 200, 28, { font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: \"#a8aac4\" });\n      var netT = wt(\"nl4\", [\"net\"], .45), fixT = wt(\"nl4\", [\"fix\"], .75), zeroT = wt(\"nl4\", [\"zero\", \"0\"], .85);\n      var pk = eBack(prog(T, n4.start, .45));\n      g.save(); g.translate(560, 590); g.rotate(-.04); g.scale(pk, pk);\n      inkRR(g, -330, -330, 660, 660, 12, C.white, 6);\n      txt(g, \"INVOICE\", -290, -260, 44, { font: COMIC, weight: 400, fill: C.ink, ls: 3 });\n      for (var r = 0; r < 5; r++) { inkLine(g, -290, -190 + r * 46, 150, -190 + r * 46, 3, \"rgba(42,36,51,.3)\"); }\n      var fixed = T > fixT, pickNet = T > netT && !fixed;\n      inkRR(g, -300, 60, 600, 80, 10, fixed ? \"#d6f1dc\" : \"#fff\", 4, fixed ? C.mintD : C.ink);\n      txt(g, \"TOTAL\", -270, 115, 40, { fill: C.ink }); txt(g, \"$\" + (ex.total || \"\"), 270, 115, 44, { align: \"right\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.ink });\n      inkRR(g, -300, 170, 600, 80, 10, pickNet ? \"#ffd9d6\" : \"#fff\", 4, pickNet ? C.red : C.ink);\n      txt(g, \"NET AMOUNT DUE\", -270, 225, 34, { fill: C.ink }); txt(g, \"$\" + (ex.net_read || \"\"), 270, 225, 44, { align: \"right\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.ink });\n      g.restore();\n      if (pickNet) { stamp(g, \"READ THE NET ✗\", 560, 520, netT + .2, C.red, 56, -.08); }\n      if (fixed) { stamp(g, \"READS THE TOTAL ✓\", 560, 520, fixT, C.mintD, 56, -.08); }\n      // the count of silent wrong totals per pass, before -> after\n      var zk = eBack(prog(T, zeroT - .3, .4));\n      if (zk > 0) {\n        g.save(); g.translate(1330, 520); g.scale(zk, zk);\n        inkRR(g, -360, -220, 720, 440, 24, C.cream, 6);\n        txt(g, \"silent wrong totals, per pass\", 0, -150, 32, { align: \"center\", fill: C.ink, weight: 700 });\n        txt(g, \"tuned-on 12:\", -320, -60, 34, { fill: C.ink, weight: 600 }); txt(g, sw.tuned_v1 + \"  →  \" + sw.tuned_v2, 320, -60, 46, { align: \"right\", fill: C.mintD });\n        txt(g, \"held-out 12:\", -320, 30, 34, { fill: C.ink, weight: 600 }); txt(g, sw.heldout_v1 + \"  →  \" + sw.heldout_v2, 320, 30, 46, { align: \"right\", fill: C.mintD });\n        txt(g, \"n = 3 passes each\", 0, 150, 26, { align: \"center\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: \"#6a6170\" });\n        g.restore();\n      }\n      sfxWord(g, \"OOPS!\", 900, 250, netT + .1, 100, C.red, -.1);\n      sfxWord(g, \"FIXED!\", 1620, 230, zeroT, 100, C.green, .1);\n      host(g, 1790, 1075, .75, [[n4.start, \"present\", \"smile\"], [netT - .1, \"point\", \"wow\", [560, 640]], [zeroT - .1, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], { face: -1, hop: zeroT });\n      confetti(g, 1330, 420, zeroT);\n      caption(g, sc, null);\n      return;\n    }\n    if (T < n3.start - .05) {\n      txt(g, \"case study 02 · rerun: 5 runs per side, same models and data\", 115, 200, 28, { font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: \"#a8aac4\" });\n      var spans = [[\"plan\", 0, .1], [\"act:read_budget\", .1, .06], [\"verify:totals\", .16, .03], [\"act:fetch_competitor\", .2, .1], [\"decide:recovery\", .3, .05, 1], [\"act:fetch_jobs\", .35, .08],\n        [\"decide:recovery\", .43, .05, 1], [\"act:classify_titles\", .48, .12], [\"decide:recovery\", .6, .05, 1], [\"audit:f_ml_ai\", .72, .1], [\"report\", .86, .1]];\n      spans.forEach(function (s, i) {\n        var y = 260 + i * 50, k = prog(T, n1.start + .1 + i * .07, .35), x0 = 560 + s[1] * 1150, w = s[2] * 1150 * eOut(k);\n        if (k <= 0) return;\n        txt(g, s[0], 520, y + 28, 26, { align: \"right\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: s[3] ? C.yellow : \"#cfd0e6\" });\n        inkRR(g, x0, y + 6, Math.max(8, w), 30, 8, s[3] ? C.orange : C.teal2, 3);\n      });\n      var three = wt(\"nl2\", [\"three\", \"3\"], .2), fix = wt(\"nl2\", [\"fix\"], .45), cut = wt(\"nl2\", [\"kept\"], .75);\n      if (T > n2.start) {\n        var mk = eOut(prog(T, n2.start, .4));\n        g.save(); g.globalAlpha = mk; inkCircle(g, 1440, 560, 230, \"rgba(20,24,48,.94)\", 8);\n        if (T < fix) {\n          txt(g, \"substitute_competitor\", 1440, 450, 27, { align: \"center\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.orange });\n          [\"Honeycomb\", \"Arize\", \"Chronosphere\"].forEach(function (nm, i) { var fly = prog(T, three + .2 + i * .2, .5); txt(g, \"✗ \" + nm, 1440 + fly * 260 * (i - 1), 520 + i * 56 - fly * 160, 38, { align: \"center\", fill: C.red, weight: 700 }); });\n          txt(g, \"→ New Relic (3,095)\", 1440, 700, 30, { align: \"center\", fill: C.cream, weight: 600 }); txt(g, \"→ Datadog (10,482)\", 1440, 740, 30, { align: \"center\", fill: C.cream, weight: 600 });\n        } else {\n          (RUN.competitors || []).forEach(function (c, i) { txt(g, \"✓ \" + c.name, 1440, 430 + i * 50, 34, { align: \"center\", fill: C.green, weight: 700 }); });\n          var c2 = FX.case02 || {};\n          txt(g, \"5 of 5 kept\", 1440, 700, 42, { align: \"center\", fill: C.yellow, weight: 700 });\n          txt(g, \"in \" + (c2.runs_per_side || 5) + \" of \" + (c2.runs_per_side || 5) + \" runs\", 1440, 745, 32, { align: \"center\", fill: C.cream, weight: 600 });\n        }\n        g.restore(); inkLine(g, 1600, 720, 1660, 790, 22, C.ink);\n        sfxWord(g, \"YOINK!\", 1220, 300, three + .4, 100, C.orange, -.12);\n        sfxWord(g, \"FIXED!\", 1700, 250, fix + .2, 100, C.green, .1);\n      }\n      /* Mao presents here */\n      host(g, 1790, 1075, 0.8, [[n1.start, \"present\", \"smile\"], [n2.start, \"point\", \"smile\", [1440, 560]], [fix, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], { face: -1, hop: fix });\n    } else {\n      txt(g, \"case study 05 · same Acme data · 5 identical runs per side\", 115, 200, 28, { font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: \"#a8aac4\" });\n      var one = wt(\"nl3\", [\"one\", \"1\"], .8), before = (FX.case05 || {}).before || [], after = (FX.case05 || {}).after || [];\n      var COL = { confirmed: C.green, overturned: C.red, downgraded: C.yellow };\n      before.forEach(function (v, i) {\n        var land = T > one + i * .08, spin = land ? eBack(prog(T, one + i * .08, .4)) : 0, cur = land ? after[i] : v;\n        var k = eBack(prog(T, n3.start + i * .1, .4)); if (k <= 0) return;\n        g.save(); g.translate(300 + i * 300, 560 + (land ? 0 : Math.sin(T * 9 + i) * 14)); g.scale(k, k); g.rotate(land ? (1 - spin) * TAU : Math.sin(T * 6 + i) * .15);\n        inkRR(g, -125, -125, 250, 250, 30, COL[cur] || C.cream, 6);\n        txt(g, \"run \" + (i + 1), 0, -70, 26, { align: \"center\", font: MONO, weight: 500, fill: C.ink }); txt(g, cur, 0, 20, 36, { align: \"center\", fill: C.ink, weight: 700 });\n        g.restore();\n      });\n      var big = T < one ? \"3 verdicts\" : \"1 verdict\";\n      txt(g, big, 960, 870, 110, { align: \"center\", font: COMIC, weight: 400, fill: T < one ? C.red : C.yellow, stroke: C.ink, sw: 14, ls: 4 });\n      sfxWord(g, \"CLICK!\", 1650, 300, one, 100, C.yellow, .1);\n      host(g, 1790, 1075, 0.8, [[n3.start, \"think\", \"think\"], [one - .1, \"cheer\", \"grin\"]], { face: -1, hop: one });\n    }\n    caption(g, sc, null);\n  };\n\n  // 07 ENTIRE — commits fall in with checkpoint stickers; a detective board traces span → code → commit → prompt; runner-bots catch 2 bugs\n  S.entire = function (g, sc) {\n    var e1 = L(\"ent1\"), e2 = L(\"ent2\"), e3 = L(\"ent3\"), X2 = FX.explain || {};\n    g.drawImage(paper(\"ent\", \"#dcd1f3\", [\"#c4b4ee\", \"#efe6ff\", \"#b6c8f0\", \"#f3d9ef\"], 113), 0, 0);\n    txt(g, \"Entire\", 110, 160, 92, { fill: C.ink });\n    if (T < e2.start - .05) {\n      (FX.commits || []).slice(0, 6).forEach(function (c, i) {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b7995ec0-322b-436d-8b6b-5338e6789283","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Computer/Coding/neathack/SpeedRadar-NeetHack/demo-video","root":"/c/Computer/Coding/neathack/SpeedRadar-NeetHack","branch":"demo-video","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modif